@page "/datagrid-composite-columns"

<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.H2" TagName="TagName.H1" class="rz-pt-8">
    Blazor DataGrid <strong>Composite Columns</strong>
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" TagName="TagName.P" class="rz-pb-4">
    Group related Blazor DataGrid columns under a shared header - also known as column bands, column groups or multi-level headers.
</RadzenText>

<RadzenText Anchor="datagrid-composite-columns#column-bands" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-8">
    Column bands
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mb-8">
    Nest columns in the <code>Columns</code> of a parent column and the parent becomes a header that spans them.
    The nested columns keep sorting, filtering and footer templates, and the same child columns can repeat under different parents.
    Set the <code>Width</code> of the parent column and its child columns share it.
</RadzenText>
<RadzenExample ComponentName="DataGrid" Example="DataGridColumnBands">
    <DataGridColumnBands />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText Anchor="datagrid-composite-columns#composite-data-cells" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-8">
    Composite data cells
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mb-8">
    By default a parent column is a header only. Set <code>AllowCompositeDataCells="true"</code> to make the data cells follow the header layout:
    a parent column with a <code>Property</code> or <code>Template</code> shows its own value in a cell that spans its child columns,
    and each record takes one table row per header level. Columns without children span all of them.
</RadzenText>

<RadzenExample ComponentName="DataGrid" Example="DataGridCompositeDataCells">
    <DataGridCompositeDataCells />
</RadzenExample>
